{\pard \qc \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \b \fs36 Terms of Service\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 {\b Last updated}: this document was rewritten for the Zode fork; it no longer describes Zed Industries, Inc.'s hosted service, subscription, or its original 40+ page Terms of Service.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 There is no service, so there are no Terms of Service\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Upstream Zed's Terms of Service governed a hosted subscription service: accounts, billing, a collaboration server, hosted AI features. This fork removed all of that \u8212- there is no service to have terms for. Zode is software you run locally.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 What actually governs your use of Zode\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 The software license does:\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "/LICENSE-GPL"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
LICENSE-GPL
}}}
} (GPL-3.0-or-later) covers the application code \u8212- {\f1 zed}, {\f1 editor}, {\f1 project}, {\f1 workspace}, {\f1 client}, and most of the rest of the crates in this repository.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "/LICENSE-APACHE"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
LICENSE-APACHE
}}}
} (Apache-2.0) covers {\f1 gpui} and a handful of related crates.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa0 \li360 \fi-360 \bullet \tx360\tab {\b {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "/NOTICE"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
NOTICE
}}}
} credits the upstream Zed project this fork comes from.\sa180\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Those licenses grant you the rights to run, study, modify, and redistribute this software, and they're the only legal terms that apply to using it. There is no Contributor License Agreement, no Code of Conduct tied to a hosted forum (this isn't a hosted product), and no arbitration clause, because there is no company on the other side of this software to have one with.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel1 \b \fs32 The one exception: the extension registry\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 Installing an extension reaches Zed Industries' extension registry ({\f1 api.zed.dev}) \u8212- a disclosed, retained third-party dependency, not part of this software's own terms. See {\f1 legal/third-party-terms.md} for what that means and {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "https://zed.dev/terms"}}{\fldrslt{\ul
Zed's own Terms of Service
}}}
 for the registry service itself. Everything else in Zode runs with no service, and therefore no terms, behind it.\par}
